Z||000009||olympic||01-04-2000||02:41 PM||||  I can honestly say that I did absolutely nothing for Y2K. No extra cash on hand, no bottled water, no statement of bank accounts...nothing. I do own a generator but I bought it many years ago.  For all the "heightened awareness" people out there the next date to be concerned with is May 5, 2000. On that day something like 7 or 8 of the nine planets will be in a straight line. I bought a book called 5/5/2000 by Richard Noone a couple years back.  The author says that the gravitational effects of this planetary alignment will cause major stresses in the earth's crust. It could even be enough to break the antarctic ice cap loose and cause it to slide over the surface of the earth. ||||reg||1
Z||000010||2M4 Dale||01-04-2000||02:56 PM||||People today should stay ready for any eventuallity. Americans, generaly, don't think that anything bad can happen here. Man OH Man are they wrong. Modern countries can and do have social/political upheavals from time to time. The Y2K thing was a joke. The retailers made out like bandits. I'm a licensed firearms dealer and my sales went through the roof. (Good for me) Take a lesson from the Boy Scouts...Stay prepaired !!! Faith in God and heaven above don't hurt anything either...HAPPY NEW CENTURY !!!||||reg||14
Z||000011||Raydar||01-04-2000||03:07 PM||||I *did* buy some water. That's about it, -and I cleaned my 9mm.<BR>Loaded two clips (in case of "civil unrest" of some sort) and headed off to babysit the computers.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Can't wait 'till all of those "barely used, $200" generators start appearing in the want-ads.||||reg||1
Z||000012||Monkeyman||01-04-2000||05:45 PM||||Everybody keeps talking about the Y2K crisis being a joke or fake or something.  The reason that nothing major happened is due to the brilliance of the computer programmers.  If it weren't for them, you guys (and Kel) would probably have had to use your guns.  Give them some credit.  They deserve a big pat on the back.<P>Shiner--My father-in-law has a Ruger Super Black Hawk .44 Magnum (7" barrel, scope).  Too much weapon for me, but cool as he!!.  All I've got is a Walther PPK (.380), a Glock 9mm (my favorite) and an Army issue .45.  Nothing fancy like the Ruger.  Mine stay loaded all the time (no kids in the house) and had nothing to do with Y2K.  As a matter of fact, they stayed locked in whatever they normally stay locked in (car, wifes purse (PPK), and lock box in the closet.||||reg||1
