Z||000017||GREENDANO||01-04-2000||11:22 PM||||My turn.  I have had a generator for a while  (more than a year)  so I did make sure I had fuel for it.  But then again, it's winter here where I am and I always make sure I have fuel for the generator, and the snowblower.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>  As far as computer rediness, I shut both my computers down, one main system and one for just my home automation, just in case we got a surge.  The main survived, 'cause I checked it, but the automation terminal had a glitch in the software that the manufacturer never bothered to fix until last night, so I had to MANUALLY turn lights on in my house.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>  No amo needed, I have a 22 that I target shoot for fun but have never considered using it for protection.  You people with the weapons for personal protection need to move.  BTW, that's a joke, no flames....  I have never worried about my wife's or my personal safety, EVER, but I live in a podunk town.<BR>  My Friday night was spent consumming a steady amount of Coors light and eating, over at a friends house across town.<BR>  Olympic, I too prescribe to the 5-5-00 theory.  I've been joking about it for a while.  Some people say it is even the coming of the seven horseman of the apocolypse.  I don't know if I would go that far, but in extreme cases, fear and ignorance in the mind can be a powerful and dangerous thing.<BR>  Dan-O<BR>||||reg||10
