Z||000020||Phaeton||01-05-2000||05:10 AM||||Lets see...fifty degrees below zero, visibility less than twenty feet, fireworks cancelled due to ice fog, if I had plumbing it would have froze.  The upside is- yesterday a young moose not more than a year away from his mom walked through the yard and spent a few minutes eating willow bark.  If the stores and trans systems had quit he would have fed me through the rest of the winter, young and tender too.  Guns are survival tools and are maintained year round.  Never had to point one at a person yet, but have had my hand on pocket gun more than one time.  Quite a few folks up here are here because of the fragility of the overcrowded world surviving on higher and higher tech with no way to go back without most of the population going also.  Ahhh  get in the Fiero..drive fast on twisty roads..ummm...me, the road, the world retreats and all is well again. <BR>  ||||reg||1
