Z||000023||JIM GOOSE||01-07-2000||12:46 PM||||I panicked several years ago when CLINTON wanted to outlaw assault rifles. I ran out to my friendly neighborhood gun show and bought #1 on his hitlist. A MAK-90 with assorted clips and lots of military ammo so could defend myself in upcoming "conflicts". I've only shot it a couple of times and have to admit it will give you a feeling of power over and above any handgun. Now with some manf. pulling back from gun market due to lawsuits, everybody's buying again. I am personally glad we didn't have any Y2K power outages cause I would have had to come into work if we had.||||reg||1
Z||000024||Monkeyman||01-07-2000||08:32 PM||||Nothing personal here, but what's the purpose of assault weapons?  You can't take it hunting.  (I mean, come on guys.  If you can't hit the damn deer with one shot, let it go!)  You can't legally carry it on your person.  I guess it would be a good idea if you're being attacked by thousands of mutant aliens, but then you might want to have a few grenades or rocket launchers, too!  I'm NOT flaming anybody, just trying to figure out the reason for these other than for a collection.  ||||reg||1
Z||000025||cobra427||01-08-2000||02:41 AM||||Monkeyman,<BR>I think the use of the term "assault weapon"is a term that the media loves to use to cast an even darker shadow on guns.Its true. A rifle (or handgun) may be used as an "assult weapon",if used improperly.But so can a foot."So and so was charged in court today,because he or she assaulted so and so with a dangerous weapon, A FOOT." Ever see that in a court report?  The rifles(flintlocks) used to fight the British were ,back then, considered "assult weapons". Today, thos same flintlocks are mainly thought of as ,collector guns,not "assult weapons".hhmmmmmmm..<P>Besides,the 2nd ammendment does not specify as to the type of gun one  could own.It does say that we have the right to keep and bare arms.This of course would not include the "law breaker" because "he" by his lawlessness, would forfiet that right ,as well "he" should. So its not a question of hunting with the large capacity rifle,but more to the point that if someone has a notion to want a military style rifle, and enjoys shooting it, then WHY NOT.<BR>    Go to Australia and try to buy even a slingshot let alone a gun of any type and see if you can. NOT!<P>     Think of this:without the second ammendment,you have no Bill of rights, and that is scary.||||reg||1
