Z||000028||Racer 1||01-08-2000||03:58 PM||||There not assualt weapons! Its just a government induced name to scare the public. A guns a gun a cars a car? I personnaly had my mak90 fully loaded and my stoner 25 loaded as well on new years. But my sons moms side of the family is kinda whacked so I didnt want any property fandalised. Nothing better then firing off 30rnds of 7.62x39  ammo for new years in the desert!||||reg||8
Z||000029||Monkeyman||01-08-2000||04:31 PM||||You're correct.  The name was introduced by the gov't.   It was introduced by the US Army during WWI (or II, whichever one had the Invasion of Normandy).  It's not a term meant for scaring the public.  Actually, it's in the dictionary.  I hadn't meant to cause a fight, but I still say that assault weapons were meant for 3 things only:  a collection, a true assault by trained, qualified individuals (SWAT, armed forces), and gang members.  Nothing personal, but if you can't defend yourself without a fully automatic weapon, you need to get to a firing range and practice.  BTW-I'd rather have my property vandalized than kill someone.  You can always replace your property.  Another BTW--If "A gun's a gun and a car's a car" were true, we'd all be happy driving Yugos.  I'm through.||||reg||1
Z||000030||Wolfhound||01-08-2000||08:49 PM||||Full automatic or as we called it "Rock and Roll" is for panic and fools. I carried an M60 thru TET and never fired more than 3 to 5 rounds at a time. Very effective. We disappeared the 273 NVA just north of Siagon. Not without cost mind you. We learned quick that noise wasn't effective and you felt a little foolish with a hot barrel and no ammo when the air was still singing with rounds.  Y2K panic to me was like pulling over to the side of the road and having a party when your car hits 100,000 miles. Silly stuff. It was a day (Period). I didn't even fix my Jamed AK47 for the party. Arming your self indeed. Ha Ha Ha Ha!!!!<BR> Oh my PH tag for my GT cost 2 bucks period.<BR>OK I,ll shut up:-)||||reg||6
