Z||000038||theogre||01-10-2000||01:37 AM||||I've listened to this long enough....... We joke around about allot of things here. This issue is no joke. (AKA Rant Time) <P>9mm is a turd, damn things can hardly put the bullet out the barrel. 223(M16-AR15) isn't much better. I'll keep my 30-30 and my Gofer Getter(22-250).<P>Some of you are aware I have my <A HREF="http://home.sprynet.com/~theogre" TARGET=_blank>own site.</A> There is a section about gun control. (The section is overdue for update) there are some links to other sites concerning the historical signifigance of weapons confiscation. (No I don't agree with all the things in some of those links.)<P>You should also look at the disasters in "Great" Britton and Australia. Now only the crooks have all but the simplest guns there. Even in Counties where guns are heavily controlled there are shootings at schools. ((Sorry Cliff, yes, I'm including the recent tragedy there in the Netherlands. I understand that boys parents are involved. That makes it even more sad.))<P>But then lets look at NYC, NY. A city where nearly all guns are prohibited. Same in Washington, DC, the murder capitol........ In NO city or state that has enacted weopons bans has crime with said weopons dropped.<P>As the NRA rightfully points out, The U.S. has hundred of laws Already On The Books that are unenforced. Unenforced that is unless you live on Ruby Ridge where FBI snipers will shoot anything that moves. And now we have a likely coverup of FBI/BATF behavior at Waco too. (((Yes I think David Koresh(sp) was looney, but Waco was another Wounded Knee at best.)))<P>Anyone that believes a government is looking for the best interest of the masses is a fool. Even Jefferson, Author of the Declaration of Independance, only really cared about his own interests. He sure as blazes didn't include his own slaves in it. It would take the civil war and a presidential assaination to free the slaves. By the way,,,, read the Emancipation Proclimation sometime..... There is no mention of slave freedom there either, altho it is a hell of a piece of speach writing. ((The E.P. and Gettysburg Address are inscribed in the interior walls of the Lincoln Memorial. A building I can't enter and leave without being in tears even after several trips. Forget the Vietnam Wall across the street. I can't get near it without wanting to scream. And no. I don't know why. I can go to about anyplace on the planet but that one.))<P>Do I agree with everything the NRA says? no. but having been a member for some time now, I can tell you that they don't have a choice but to take a zero control stance. Truth is that 99.someting plus percent of members are the people you live next door to.<P>Those of you U.S. gun owners that aren't yet NRA member should be.<P>NRA is the only internationally recognized provider of firearms training in the U.S. other than the U.S. Millitary.<P>NRA certified trainers teach 90%+ of the police in the U.S. And practically evry other shooter/hunter safety/skill program.<P>NRA certified trainers go thru MORE training than most millitaries anywhere in the world and are constantly in training or they loose their certification. ((I was thinking of becoming one myself but few people have the amount of time involved in gaining this tittle.))<P>NRA's Eddie Eagle firearm safety materials are available to any school that wants them. These materials, with the exception of copyright notice, make NO mention at all of the NRA. Eddie Eagle says(the short form): Leave it alone! Tell an Adult!<P>||||reg||1
Z||000039||stsmithgt||01-10-2000||04:48 PM||||I'm not hip on all the new laws out this year, but I took off my 30 round magazine off my SKS because I think "they" said I'd be a felon if I left it on.  So I bought 50 stripper clips.  With a good lube on the clips, you can fill that 10 round mag pretty fast.  I'm SICK of these people who think that no guns means less crime.  I get a lot of entertainment out of my SKS and pistles.  It's a form of controlled power which I thrive on.  It relates to a powerfull car.  If you compare a vehicle as an "assault" weapon,  you should be terrified at all the people who are so untrained driving around at high speeds.  Some teenager died the other day when drag racing in San Jose, CA.  Trees can be very unforgiving. Oops sorry. too much blah blah blah <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000040||GT Bastard||01-10-2000||04:52 PM||||I hear what you're saying Ogre... Even though we talk loosely about guns, I think that some of the posts on this thread make many of us(including myself) sound irresponsible when it comes to gun safety(event though that may not be the case.) Truthfully, I would never even load my gun in my apartment, and I treat it with the utmost respect.  I mean, think about it: It has the potential to end a life with 5lbs. of index finger pressure.  That's a scary fact, but it's also part of the reason that I own a gun.  I don't want to become the victim if my home is ever violated. It's entertaining to read these posts, but thanks for bringing me back to reality Ogre.  Stay safe everyone!   ||||reg||1
Z||000041||Cliff Pennock||01-11-2000||05:52 PM||||I live in a country where carrying a gun on the street is a felony, and so is owning one without the proper certifications and without having separate vaults to store both the gun and its ammo. I also live in a country where if I catch a burglar in my house and I beat the crap out of him, <B>I</B> will go to jail while the burglar probably walks. This same country jails a police-officer that shot a guy who was attacking him with a big knife.<P>I live in a country where the police is afraid to do anything, because of the fear of landing in jail, and because the police is absolutely outgunned by the criminals. The police carries Walter P9's, arguably the worst and unreliable gun in the world.<P>Our problem is what we call "senseless violence". A lot of kids today carry guns on the street. These kids are given the feeling they can do anything, because no police-officer is going to stop them. Today, a seventeen-year old kid died because he was simply at the wrong place at the wrong time. He was attacked for no reason at all, and was beaten to death while his girlfriend watched. Last year two teenage girls died because somebody felt it necessary to empty his gun in a crowded bar.<P>Sometimes these guys get caught. But at best, they'll face 4 years in prison (if they'll go to prison at all).<P>We have a huge problem with crime here in Holland, but it is kept very quiet. I live downtown a major city and at least once a week there is some shooting going on on my own doorstep. As far as I know, one girl was killed last year (the daughter of one of my neighbors), and several other people had been shot but survived. Not once have I seen it mentioned in the paper or in the news. Why? Because then our government has to admit that their measurements against crime are insufficient. And they'll have to explain to the people why they jail police-officers.<P>Holland has created a no-win situation. By outlawing guns, criminals can almost do whatever they want because no-one (including the police) is going to stop them. And if they let anybody carry guns, it would mean total anarchy.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Cliff Pennock (edited 01-11-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000042||cobra427||01-12-2000||02:00 AM||||Hi Cliff, Out of curiosity, what form of govt does Holland have?  It seems to me that if the people of Holland have the chance to make decisions at the ballot box,it would behove them to start making a few changes in the near future. Unfortunately, the apparthy of the people in ones country can only lead to the demise of its citizens.Hopefully its not to late in this country yet. <BR> Sorry to hear that you have been made one of the "victims of our times".||||reg||5
Z||000043||RFMike||01-12-2000||11:39 PM||||Alright, this is a long way from Fieros, but I'm going to jump in.<BR>One of you suggested moving to the upper Midwest.  Well, that's where I live, and it isn't exempt from crime.  About two years ago, the headlines were about three teenagers who followed an older couple home that had been at a casino.  They came home with 10 bucks, but the punks thought they had a load.  They shot them both in the head.  This was in a farmhouse, in a very picturesque little valley.<BR>The chances of this happening are remote, but  not impossible, even in this area.  And yes, we have good cops.  Some of my best friends investigated and cracked this case.<P>What I would suggest for most people that want home defense is a shotgun.  You don't have to be a great shot, and the stopping power of a 12 gauge 3" magnum with goose shot at short range is nearly unbelievable.  There really isn't a pistol made that compares.<BR>From a legal standpoint, you are much less likely to lose a lawsuit if you are defending yourself with a true hunting weapon, rather than a weapon that is viewed by the public as  paramilitary.  <BR>For those of you that say it is too slow, spend some time shooting traps.  The speed you can develop with a long gun will surprise you.  Also, you can have a short barrel (but keep it legal)on it at home, which is actually better for self defense.<BR>I think that if every home had a gun in it, we wouldn't have burglaries.<BR>That said, sorry to hear about your loss, Cliff.  I'm even sorrier that you probably can't do anything about it.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000044||Cooter||01-12-2000||11:57 PM||||I live in Alabama. Not everything myth about my state is true! But some are. Recently a group of thugs walked into a Shoneys, drew guns and started herding the people into the cooler. One customer had a Colt 1911 45 automatic and was able to save countless people's lives. I believe one punk got away, one was DOA and the other will crap in a bag attached to his side for the rest of his life- I'm sure getting gut-shot 3 times with a 45 was not his idea of a good evening. My brother had the duty of standing outside the injured punk's hospital room. In the hospital room, the punk started to cry and told everybody that he wasn't going to hurt anybody, he didn't deserve to get shot over what he did! Poor Baby. <p>[This message has been edited by Cooter (edited 01-13-2000).]||||reg||1
